// THE PUNTERS' MOVES (Run the Pub): a library of keyframed body animations for the people in the pub, ~80 of them:
// standing about with a pint, queueing at the bar (waving for service, drumming fingers, tapping a foot, getting the
// card out, fuming), sat at the tables (chatting, laughing, toasts, a story with the arms going, a kid swinging their
// legs), dancing, watching the telly and the darts, and the big ones: proper FIGHTING (squaring up, shoves, jabs,
// haymakers, uppercuts, taking one, grappling, held back, falling about), proper ARGUING (pointing, the finger in the
// chest, arms wide, counting the points off, face to face, storming off) and proper SINGING (belting it out, pint in
// the air, chanting, an arm round your mate, conducting the whole pub).
//
// A clip is a list of keys: [time, { channel: value }]. Each channel is eased (smootherstep) from key to key on its
// own, so a key only lists what moves then. Channels (all in the body's own frame, +Z forward, +Y up):
//   aL / aR   an arm: [upper arm direction, forearm direction] (x is OUTWARD for both arms: mirrored for the right)
//   lL / lR   a leg, the same (thigh, shin)
//   ch / pe   the chest / hips turned: [lean forward, turn left, tip to the right] (radians)
//   hd        the head: [look down, look left, tilt]
//   bob       the hips up (+) or down (-) in metres, fz forward (+) / back (-)
// Sat down, only the arms, chest and head play (the legs stay on the seat). Changing clip cross-fades over 0.6s, every
// person plays at their own pace (and one in seven is left-handed: mirrored), so a pub full of them never moves as one.
import * as THREE from 'three';

